From 9d65c9b58c02f68a40e68fc099522b93ed0922e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 19:22:44 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(setup): pick the work offset (G54-G59) a setup posts at

A setup now stores its program offset (SetupDef.work_offset, default
Auto = the inferred per-operation law, so every existing document and
golden posts byte-identically). The one slot law, wcs_slot(world, setup,
params), reads the pick first; wcs_context and every caller (generation,
stamp, spindle law, machine travel check, the post, the #315 rotation
clause) follow it.

- SetSetupWorkOffset: undoable, validated at construction; a datum
  transfer copies the source's pick.
- Setups page: a Work offset combo per setup (Auto, G54..G59).
- Project v51: "work_offset": "G55" on the setup payload, omitted when
  unpicked; v50 steps up (absent = Auto); an unknown word is corrupt.
- Refusals by name: a height measured from another slot than its
  setup's pick (verification gate); two setups of one NC file posting
  the same word from different placements (one-file/script post; per-op
  files exempt).
- Setup sheet: WCS OFFSETS names the program offset.

Fixes #196

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
